(6159766, 907770, 112292, '<td valign="top">Very nice idea. I like it. 8</td>', 'Very nice idea. I like it. 8', '2010-09-12 14:38:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6159768, 907797, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''m reviewing this challenge a second time after considering what the s-curve technique is really supposed to be. Though an S-curve is clearly visible in this, I don''t find that it functions as an element that leads my eye to the subject. If anything, my eye lands first on the subject of the fork head, and  the s-curve attempts to pull my eye <i>away</i> from it. One of the more interesting fork shots I have seen however. What is creating that criss cross pattern in the backgound?</td>', 'I''m reviewing this challenge a second time after considering what the s-curve technique is really supposed to be. Though an S-curve is clearly visible in this, I don''t find that it functions as an element that leads my eye to the subject. If anything, my eye lands first on the subject of the fork head, and  the s-curve attempts to pull my eye away from it. One of the more interesting fork shots I have seen however. What is creating that criss cross pattern in the backgound?', '2010-09-12 14:41:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6159770, 907696, 108069, '<td valign="top">I''m not voting in this challenge as I''m in it. I think this a fantastic photo, but I have to be completely honest and tell you I am tired of this scene. I''ve seen this bridge in far too many challenges. It''s interesting, no doubt. Well executed, no doubt. But I just don''t know how many more times I can see this get high votes. Sorry, but does that make sense? (Again, not voting; just feedback.)</td>', 'I''m not voting in this challenge as I''m in it. I think this a fantastic photo, but I have to be completely honest and tell you I am tired of this scene. I''ve seen this bridge in far too many challenges. It''s interesting, no doubt. Well executed, no doubt. But I just don''t know how many more times I can see this get high votes. Sorry, but does that make sense? (Again, not voting; just feedback.)', '2010-09-12 14:42:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6159771, 907850, 108069, '<td valign="top">Great texture. Great contrast.</td>', 'Great texture. Great contrast.', '2010-09-12 14:42:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6159773, 907830, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''m reviewing this challenge a second time after considering what the s-curve technique is really supposed to be. I''m rather marginal on whether this completely fits my definition, but I do find my eye is somewhat led from the egret''s body up the neck to it''s head. I''ll let my earlier vote stand.</td>', 'I''m reviewing this challenge a second time after considering what the s-curve technique is really supposed to be. I''m rather marginal on whether this completely fits my definition, but I do find my eye is somewhat led from the egret''s body up the neck to it''s head. I''ll let my earlier vote stand.', '2010-09-12 14:43:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6159774, 906579, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like the abstract patterns of this, and I do find the s-curves work to lead my eye up the frame.</td>', 'I like the abstract patterns of this, and I do find the s-curves work to lead my eye up the frame.', '2010-09-12 14:44:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6159778, 907573, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''m reviewing this challenge a second time after considering what the s-curve technique is really supposed to be. That is a compositional technique used to lead the viewer into the image. Though it''s very curvy, I''m not totally sure if there is an eye leading s-curve in here. I find my eye actually being led in a fairly straight line up to to the second level of the foreground structure. (Curse me as a DPC nitpicker, if you like.)</td>', 'I''m reviewing this challenge a second time after considering what the s-curve technique is really supposed to be. That is a compositional technique used to lead the viewer into the image. Though it''s very curvy, I''m not totally sure if there is an eye leading s-curve in here. I find my eye actually being led in a fairly straight line up to to the second level of the foreground structure. (Curse me as a DPC nitpicker, if you like.)', '2010-09-12 14:49:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6159780, 907826, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''m reviewing this challenge a second time after considering what the s-curve technique is really supposed to be. That is a compositional technique used to lead the viewer into the image. Though there ar obvious s-curves in these insturments I''m not totally sure if there is an eye leading s-curve here. Very nice shot however, and ultimately that''s what matters. My apologies if you find me overly nitpicky on the definition of the topic.</td>', 'I''m reviewing this challenge a second time after considering what the s-curve technique is really supposed to be. That is a compositional technique used to lead the viewer into the image. Though there ar obvious s-curves in these insturments I''m not totally sure if there is an eye leading s-curve here. Very nice shot however, and ultimately that''s what matters. My apologies if you find me overly nitpicky on the definition of the topic.', '2010-09-12 14:51:25.000000', NULL, 1),
